{"kind":"request","text":"Archive capacity: the numeric capture build (child of 0f0eeab7).\n\nYes to d28ab5ba: the capture build lands as its own reviewed head over\nMain 33690b69, and 0f0eeab7 stays open for the measurement note and\nany justified cost cut.\n\nWork: the bounded closed numeric capture as proposed in cbdf2559 and\naccepted in 6634c94c item 4: reuse the values already computed at\nplanningRowContext, forecastArchiveFinish and the plan result, before\nexport or body selection; emit only exact target sequence and hash,\nrow and row-context byte lengths, entry, reference and declaration\ngeometry, parent object count and bytes, source lookup cost,\npreparation forecast counters, component cost vectors and the terminal\nused, requested, reserved and shortfall; charged byte geometry for\nparent path names, never the names. No new endpoint, authority\nexception, budget change, directive or deployment; the default\nproduction budget only.\n\nConditions: one head; ordinary gate at the exact head; PD-2 note and\nmanifest; named witnesses with paired controls for completeness (the\ncaptured total equals fixedFinish.remaining and the captured first\nquote equals fixedFinish.used), privacy (no body, signature, token,\nheader, setting or object content in any emitted record; a control\nthat adds one byte of content fails) and debit preservation (every\ncharge the production plan debits is debited unchanged with the\ncapture on); every measurement labelled by how it was taken; one\nchecker review at the exact head before landing; no builder deploy.\n\nAfter landing the planner deploys dap-grow from the files with\n--keep-vars, waits for turnover, reads each row's current next entry\n(sequence and hash) and the numeric diagnostic records, and files them\nunder 0f0eeab7 for the comparison. A refused next entry is identified\nby the immutable hash from the planner's bounded metadata read; no\nentry body is retained.","body":{"conditions":"One head over Main 33690b69 o